---
/**
 * NAVIGATION SIGNPOST — not the redesigned Columna-as-system page.
 *
 * Authorized narrowly (Huayin, 2026-08-19): a concise current definition plus links to the Columna
 * surfaces that are already live. No route is migrated and nothing here is rebuilt — every
 * destination below is an existing page, unchanged.
 *
 * The upward-framing line is the bidirectional rule in miniature: a product surface points back to
 * the principle that explains why the behaviour exists.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const SURFACES = [
  { href: '/install', label: 'Install and run the demo',
    blurb: 'a clarify, a refuse and a disclose print on your own machine, as wire JSON.' },
  { href: '/learn', label: 'Learn the framework',
    blurb: 'what Columna, Frame-QL and a Manifold are — and the three manuals.' },
  { href: '/explorer', label: 'The Manifold Explorer',
    blurb: 'browse the Cascadia Manifold: universes, measures, verdicts.' },
  { href: '/docs/frameql', label: 'The Frame-QL manual',
    blurb: 'the language of governed meaning, in full.' },
  { href: '/case', label: 'The worked case',
    blurb: 'a realistic warehouse, the Manifold that serves it, and recorded agent transcripts.' },
  { href: 'https://github.com/datumwise/columna', label: 'GitHub', external: true,
    blurb: 'Apache-2.0, open source.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Columna — datumwise"
  description="Columna is an open-source analytical system in which governed meaning, not physical procedure, determines what may be served."
  chip={false}
>
  <p class="ds-label">Columna</p>

  <h1 class="ds-proposition">
    Governed meaning, not physical procedure, determines what may be served.
  </h1>

  <p class="lede ds-body">
    Columna is an open-source analytical system: a declared model of what the data means, a query
    language that can only ask for meaning the model declares, and an engine that serves nothing the
    model cannot defend.
  </p>

  <ul class="surfaces">
    {SURFACES.map((s) => (
      <li>
        <a href={s.href} {...(s.external ? { rel: 'noopener', target: '_blank' } : {})}>{s.label}</a>
        <span class="blurb"> — {s.blurb}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="upward">
    These behaviours are not product personality. They follow from the rule that absence of
    contradiction is not permission. <a href="/analytical-governance">Analytical Governance →</a>
  </p>

  <p class="status">
    This page is a navigation signpost onto surfaces that already exist. The Columna-as-system
    page — overview, Frame-QL, Core, Platform, build — is a later slice of the redesign.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ds-label { margin: 3rem 0 1.25rem; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 2rem; }
  .lede { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }

  .surfaces { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .surfaces li {
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
  }
  .surfaces a { color: var(--ink); }
  .blurb { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .upward {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .status {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--ds-meta);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
